Done. T051 implemented in one file.

## Files written

- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`
  - `spawnTurn(runtime, argv, prompt, capMs, ghConfig)` now takes the prompt and sets `stdio[0]` to `'pipe'` when the runtime's row has `promptOnStdin: true`, `'ignore'` otherwise.
  - When a stdin pipe exists: one `error` listener (a CLI that exits before reading leaves a broken pipe, which must not surface as an uncaught write error), then `child.stdin.end(prompt)` — written and closed in one call so a CLI reading to end-of-input sees the whole prompt.
  - Call site updated: `spawnTurn(job.runtime, argv, job.prompt, job.cap, job.ghConfig)`.
  - Comment hygiene kept: WHY only, no spec/phase/task ids.

